ccumulation.\n\nBreakdown of +48: Comprehensive +25 (55→80), Occupational Test +21 (55→76–80). Hmm, the goal is 160; if Comprehensive is 80 then Occupational Test needs to be 80. Realistically: Comprehensive 78–80, Occupational Test 80–82.\n\nDaily 4-hour plan for a working adult: e.g., weekdays 4 hours: 1 hour Comprehensive method study, 1.5 hours Occupational Test specialized drills, 1 hour past problem practice, 0.5 hours current affairs/error review. Weekends with extra time can go longer.\n\nLet's update the files. Plan:\n1. Replace the mnemon user entry.\n2. Edit the diagnostic section of 00-Exam Prep Overview.md + rewrite the weekly rhythm.\n3. Edit the rows in score tracking.md + tentatively fill in the score-boosting path.\n4. Might create a detailed weekly plan file 06-Study Plan/Week 1 Plan.md — but keep it simple; put the 4-hour daily template in the overview, and propose starting the diagnostic phase on Monday.\n\nAlso propose the start of the diagnostic phase: since they've already taken many exams and their weaknesses are identified, the diagnostic phase might only need one baseline Comprehensive practice set (the Occupational Test weaknesses are already known). Actually, the user has taken many exams so they have a sense of it, but a module-by-module precise accuracy diagnosis is still useful. However, it might be OK to skip a full diagnostic phase and start immediately. My proposal: on this weekend, take one past Zhejiang unified exam (Occupational Test + Comprehensive) with timing, to calibrate module-by-module accuracy rates — since they're employed, do it on the weekend.\n\nNow let's make the edits.\n"}}, {"type": "block-start", "index": 1, "blockType": "text"}, {"type": "text-delta", "index": 1, "text": "\n"}, {"type": "text-delta", "index": 1, "text": "Great, the information"}, {"type": "text-delta", "index": 1, "text": " is very"}, {"type": "text-delta", "index": 1, "text": " complete. The breakthrough"}, {"type": "text-delta", "index": 1, "te